Here's the full `#onScmEvents` method and the code invoking `markEventActionTaken`.

## The `#onScmEvents` method

This method processes an array of SCM events. It begins by declaring collections to track pending actions:

```js
const exactLocationsToDelete = new Set<string>();
const locationPrefixesToDelete = new Set<string>();
const exactLocationsToCreate = new Set<string>();
const locationPrefixesToMove = new Map<string, string>();
```

It then iterates over events, routing each based on type and config flags:

- `'location.deleted'` (when `unregister` is on) → adds `event.url` to `exactLocationsToDelete`
- `'location.moved'` (when `move` is on) → adds `event.fromUrl` to deletions and `event.toUrl` to creations, because as the comment notes, "Location entities are named after their target URL, these unfortunately have to be translated into deletion and creation"
- `'repository.deleted'` (when `unregister` is on) → adds `event.url` to `locationPrefixesToDelete`
- `'repository.moved'` (when `move` is on) → sets `event.fromUrl → event.toUrl` in `locationPrefixesToMove`

## The four `markEventActionTaken` invocations

Each pending collection, if non-empty, triggers a corresponding helper and then reports the count. Here is the exact surrounding context for all four calls:

```js
    if (exactLocationsToDelete.size > 0) {
      const count = await this.#deleteLocationsByExactUrl(
        exactLocationsToDelete,
      );
      this.scmEvents.markEventActionTaken({
        count,
        action: 'delete',
      });
    }
    if (locationPrefixesToDelete.size > 0) {
      const count = await this.#deleteLocationsByUrlPrefix(
        locationPrefixesToDelete,
      );
      this.scmEvents.markEventActionTaken({
        count,
        action: 'delete',
      });
    }
    if (exactLocationsToCreate.size > 0) {
      const count = await this.#createLocationsByExactUrl(
        exactLocationsToCreate,
      );
      this.scmEvents.markEventActionTaken({
        count,
        action: 'create',
      });
    }
    if (locationPrefixesToMove.size > 0) {
      const count = await this.#moveLocationsByUrlPrefix(
        locationPrefixesToMove,
      );
      this.scmEvents.markEventActionTaken({
        count,
        action: 'move',
      });
    }
```

## Summary of the four calls

| Guard condition | Helper called | `action` value |
|---|---|---|
| `exactLocationsToDelete.size > 0` | `#deleteLocationsByExactUrl` | `'delete'` |
| `locationPrefixesToDelete.size > 0` | `#deleteLocationsByUrlPrefix` | `'delete'` |
| `exactLocationsToCreate.size > 0` | `#createLocationsByExactUrl` | `'create'` |
| `locationPrefixesToMove.size > 0` | `#moveLocationsByUrlPrefix` | `'move'` |

In every case, `count` is the return value of the corresponding helper, and it is passed to `markEventActionTaken` along with the matching `action` string. The only method that invokes `markEventActionTaken` is `#onScmEvents`.

